Detach swupdate's stdin/stdout/stderr from the console when started via
the SysV init script, using start-stop-daemon's --background option
(the same mechanism used by Buildroot's S80swupdate). This prevents
swupdate's console_notifier output from appearing on screen. Messages
sent via syslog()/-L are unaffected, since syslog() writes to /dev/log
independently of stdio.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distro-specific init-script behavior]
Signed-off-by: Ezurio

--- a/swupdate
+++ b/swupdate
@@ -57,7 +57,11 @@
 	*)
 		echo "Starting $DESC ..."
 		cd /home/root
-		exec $DAEMON &
+		# Detach stdin/stdout/stderr from the console so console_notifier
+		# output does not appear on screen; syslog/-L are unaffected.
+		start-stop-daemon --start --quiet --background \
+			--make-pidfile --pidfile "$PIDFILE" \
+			--exec "$DAEMON"
 		exit 0
 		;;
 	esac
